# .fingerprintignore — sources that legitimately differ between this checkout and
# the EAS builder, and must not feed the expo-updates runtime-version fingerprint.
#
# 1. node_modules/react-native-audio-api — the builder runs `pod install`, which
#    writes generated files inside this package before EAS recomputes the
#    fingerprint, so its dir hash can never match a machine that only ran
#    `npm install`. Ignoring the source keeps the two fingerprints equal.
# 2. ios/** — the native dir expo prebuild generates (git-ignored). EAS prebuilds
#    before recomputing, so any local difference in generated code would shift the
#    hash; the JS bundle runtime is fully described by the package + app config
#    sources that remain included.
ios/**/*
node_modules/react-native-audio-api/**/*
